                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6bdf4dea-054a-3564-8e54-a0fc6795e281",
                        "entry_id": "90cbb1fb-b9d6-3440-970b-45727da58835",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Person, die zur Boheme gehört; jemand, der sich als unbürgerlicher/unkonventioneller Künstler aufführt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "42db5de7-1c8d-4522-a277-2bd289560161",
                                "sense_id": "6bdf4dea-054a-3564-8e54-a0fc6795e281",
                                "text": "„Nicht nur der Münchner Bohemien machte sich im Frühjahr 1915 düstere Gedanken; flächendeckend breitete sich Skepsis aus.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bca1c011-fef1-4e7a-bf7c-ecfba4e70df2",
                                "sense_id": "6bdf4dea-054a-3564-8e54-a0fc6795e281",
                                "text": "„Dennoch blieb Gershwin zeit seines Lebens ein individualistischer Bohemien.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "04a765f7-0e75-4d5a-9617-3b11cc0fcea5",
                                "sense_id": "6bdf4dea-054a-3564-8e54-a0fc6795e281",
                                "text": "„Die Kunstgeschichte hat ihn zwar (nicht ganz grundlos) mit Mißachtung gestraft, aber der damals 33jährige – mit großer Künstlerschleife und einem breiten Schlapphut als Bohemien durch die Stadt bummelnd – war für seine jugendlichen Bewunderer offenbar eine charismatische Persönlichkeit.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3e5b5ca4-b9f1-45bb-a80f-05776ad26d60",
                        "source_entry_id": "90cbb1fb-b9d6-3440-970b-45727da58835",
                        "source_sense_id": "6bdf4dea-054a-3564-8e54-a0fc6795e281",
                        "source_sense_description": "Person, die zur Boheme gehört; jemand, der sich als unbürgerlicher/unkonventioneller Künstler aufführt",
                        "target_lang_word": "bohemian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bohemian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce1eade6-1f67-3fe8-820f-083fd02f3310",
                                        "entry_id": "8cb1cad5-409d-3a46-82dc-21b8f83a254b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person, especially an artist or writer, who lives an unconventional or nonconformist lifestyle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7763732-b4cd-49cf-8866-ea195f6ad6af",
                                                "sense_id": "ce1eade6-1f67-3fe8-820f-083fd02f3310",
                                                "text": "Burlington, where Mr. Twitchell grew up and where he now spends summers, was singled out by David Brooks in his wickedly funny “Bobos in Paradise” as a model Latte Town, a city that has perfectly reconciled the mercenary instincts of the bourgeoisie with the artistic spirit of the bohemians to create an upscale consumer culture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0df48ae0-baa7-490c-b28d-88060e356dc5",
                                                "sense_id": "ce1eade6-1f67-3fe8-820f-083fd02f3310",
                                                "text": "During 1940–1941, the few Hollywood bohemians that did appear received \"harsher\" depictions. The United States' preparations for and eventual entry into World War II figured prominently in this decline and change in the treatment of Hollywood bohemians."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24bb6606-3b13-47d0-9e49-87a233464b89",
                                                "sense_id": "ce1eade6-1f67-3fe8-820f-083fd02f3310",
                                                "text": "Whitman was, by no means, the \"King of Bohemia\"—that title went to Henry Clapp Jr., the founding editor of the Saturday Press—but the bohemians embraced and supported him at a crucial moment in his career."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bohemian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f8b4c1e-4b0e-3c0c-80eb-ce66c75d09c9",
                                        "entry_id": "287a5324-337d-3a2a-a90b-19c5151c0dc7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unconventional, especially in habit or dress."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5e9267c-1ddb-488e-9ff0-cfcdea333612",
                                                "sense_id": "4f8b4c1e-4b0e-3c0c-80eb-ce66c75d09c9",
                                                "text": "2001, Baz Luhrmann, Craig Pearce (scriptwriters), Moulin Rouge!,\nPlease tell me you're not one of Toulouse's oh-so-talented, charmingly bohemian, tragically impoverished protégés!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9214ba9-ef58-4a89-b87d-74a4d37d3d27",
                                                "sense_id": "4f8b4c1e-4b0e-3c0c-80eb-ce66c75d09c9",
                                                "text": "Cowell's earlier, more bohemian years are not only the most interesting, they comprise the only part of his life for which one could reasonably attempt to do the kind of work that I have tried to do here."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b88824d-69f3-4ff5-ace9-6b3fd94637c6",
                                                "sense_id": "4f8b4c1e-4b0e-3c0c-80eb-ce66c75d09c9",
                                                "text": "Georgetown, a Jesuit university and a \"hot big city school\" (Mathews 2007:53): is popularly believed to be \"hotter,\" wealthier, more bohemian, more liberal, and more laid back than its secular counterpart, GWU."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b82c7148-fd69-4f2b-b324-7c22325d411e",
                                                "sense_id": "4f8b4c1e-4b0e-3c0c-80eb-ce66c75d09c9",
                                                "text": "The magazine's aesthetic also bends it into more bohemian territory. Food articles often have botanical illustrations of lesser-eaten greenery like endive and watercress, drawn by artist John Burgoyne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
